WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:01.627
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:01.627 --> 00:00:05.311
Today's message is "Take Criticism."

00:00:05.311 --> 00:00:07.161
Over to you, Virat Kohli.

00:00:07.161 --> 00:00:09.244
(whoosh)

00:00:10.499 --> 00:00:12.038
(rooster crowing)

00:00:12.038 --> 00:00:13.454
(funky music)

00:00:13.454 --> 00:00:15.139
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:19.519
♫ And Entspresso keep me going

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:22.184
- When I was criticized, the
first time I played for India,

00:00:22.184 --> 00:00:25.160
I was criticized for
not being disciplined,

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.808
and not being that
focused, as I had to be.

00:00:28.808 --> 00:00:32.852
So, I ignored that during the first part,

00:00:32.852 --> 00:00:35.359
'cause I thought, "okay,
I'm going to perform,

00:00:35.359 --> 00:00:37.912
so all these things
don't have to bother me."

00:00:37.912 --> 00:00:40.556
But, yeah I mean, if
someone criticizes you,

00:00:40.556 --> 00:00:42.919
it's better to actually take the criticism

00:00:42.919 --> 00:00:43.752
and look into it.

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:46.051
If something's wrong, and
you try to correct it,

00:00:46.051 --> 00:00:49.013
rather than just being blind
and just ignoring the world,

00:00:49.013 --> 00:00:53.277
and yeah, I looked upon it,
because I was out of the team,

00:00:53.277 --> 00:00:54.836
after that, for a while.

00:00:54.836 --> 00:00:59.070
And I sat and I analyzed what I did wrong,

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:00.942
and improved on a lot of things,

00:01:00.942 --> 00:01:04.751
and it was good that I
decided to take that criticism

00:01:04.751 --> 00:01:07.484
and actually change the stuff I needed to.

00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:08.995
- I think criticism is
a double-edged sword.

00:01:08.995 --> 00:01:11.873
I think, on the one hand,

00:01:11.873 --> 00:01:13.879
if all you do is listen to other people,

00:01:13.879 --> 00:01:16.187
then you're never going
to be really who you are.

00:01:16.187 --> 00:01:17.020
Right?

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.147
You're just going to be living to

00:01:18.147 --> 00:01:19.500
other people's expectations.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.333
You're just going to be doing things

00:01:20.333 --> 00:01:21.718
because other people tell you that

00:01:21.718 --> 00:01:23.121
that's what you're supposed to do,

00:01:23.121 --> 00:01:25.086
and that is never going to be the path

00:01:25.086 --> 00:01:27.802
for you to really be amazing at something.

00:01:27.802 --> 00:01:28.635
But on the other hand,

00:01:28.635 --> 00:01:30.141
you don't have all the answers, either.

00:01:30.141 --> 00:01:30.974
Right?

00:01:30.974 --> 00:01:34.250
You have a path that you're
going down, and you need help.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.302
To figure it out.

00:01:35.302 --> 00:01:36.911
And you're going to make mistakes.

00:01:36.911 --> 00:01:39.311
Not everything you do is going
to be perfect and amazing.

00:01:39.311 --> 00:01:42.660
And so it's, being able to
understand the difference.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.702
Being able to understand
what the feedback is

00:01:44.702 --> 00:01:47.912
that's going to help you get
to the path that you want,

00:01:47.912 --> 00:01:49.647
and ignore the rest.

00:01:49.647 --> 00:01:51.894
I think it's really important
that you use criticism

00:01:51.894 --> 00:01:54.259
as a counselor, but not a jailer.

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:56.812
A lot of times, people
use criticism as a jailer.

00:01:56.812 --> 00:01:59.351
Where, they're afraid to do something

00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:01.568
because somebody else
doesn't agree with them.

00:02:01.568 --> 00:02:04.247
Because somebody thinks
that your video is bad,

00:02:04.247 --> 00:02:05.662
now you're not going to post it.

00:02:05.662 --> 00:02:08.018
Now you're never going to
post another video again.

00:02:08.018 --> 00:02:09.863
Because of one person's opinion.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:12.653
And I've had people tell me
that some of my videos are bad.

00:02:12.653 --> 00:02:15.853
My famous story about how
the Littleman was created.

00:02:15.853 --> 00:02:19.300
Industry executives said
that the video was too long,

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:20.556
and should be cut down,

00:02:20.556 --> 00:02:22.965
and here it is, over
a million views later,

00:02:22.965 --> 00:02:25.156
coming up on two million views.

00:02:25.156 --> 00:02:26.674
I didn't listen to him.

00:02:26.674 --> 00:02:28.074
He's the expert.

00:02:28.074 --> 00:02:29.493
But I didn't listen to him,

00:02:29.493 --> 00:02:31.756
because it felt like I
needed to go and do this.

00:02:31.756 --> 00:02:33.720
Even just to prove to myself.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.073
Even just to try it.

00:02:35.073 --> 00:02:36.060
But there's been other times,

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.914
when industry experts have given me advice

00:02:37.914 --> 00:02:40.079
on how to be a better speaker,
how to be a better YouTuber,

00:02:40.079 --> 00:02:41.132
how to come up with better points,

00:02:41.132 --> 00:02:43.915
how to be more effective on-stage.

00:02:43.915 --> 00:02:46.198
So being able to understand the difference

00:02:46.198 --> 00:02:48.673
between the feedback
that will help you grow,

00:02:48.673 --> 00:02:51.573
and the feedback that, whoa,
I think isn't important,

00:02:51.573 --> 00:02:53.370
and that comes from experience.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:55.749
And it comes from being able
to listen to your gut, right?

00:02:55.749 --> 00:02:56.813
Trust in your heart.

00:02:56.813 --> 00:02:59.242
Almost all the feedback
that I've gotten from people

00:02:59.242 --> 00:03:00.990
that have made me better,

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.762
was almost never exactly
what I needed to hear.

00:03:04.762 --> 00:03:09.700
I had to take their advice, try
it, right, if you're unsure,

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.531
if you think maybe it's just
your ego getting in your way,

00:03:11.531 --> 00:03:13.967
then try it, and see how it works,

00:03:13.967 --> 00:03:15.983
and then I always have
to make a tweak to it.

00:03:15.983 --> 00:03:17.833
I remember I had a media
coach for two years

00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:19.943
helping me with my videos,
helping me get better,

00:03:19.943 --> 00:03:22.159
helping me improve on camera.

00:03:22.159 --> 00:03:24.455
And all of her advice was so amazing,

00:03:24.455 --> 00:03:26.913
but always seen through her own lens.

00:03:26.913 --> 00:03:30.743
And I always had to take
that advice, and adjust it.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.171
I would try what she asked me to do,

00:03:33.171 --> 00:03:35.861
and I never succeeded
at doing it (laughs).

00:03:35.861 --> 00:03:38.079
It felt uncomfortable, it felt awkward,

00:03:38.079 --> 00:03:42.002
it felt like it wasn't me,
but I appreciate the push.

00:03:42.002 --> 00:03:44.752
And from that push, I hit a wall,

00:03:45.921 --> 00:03:48.188
and then I swerved and
made my way through.

00:03:48.188 --> 00:03:50.502
I grew, and I had to figure out on my own

00:03:50.502 --> 00:03:53.536
how to make what she had
given me, that advice,

00:03:53.536 --> 00:03:57.782
and make it better, make it
more me, 'cause she can't be me,

00:03:57.782 --> 00:03:58.987
to make me better.

00:03:58.987 --> 00:04:00.791
Just like when you model success.

00:04:00.791 --> 00:04:03.055
If you look up to Steve
Jobs or Oprah Winfrey

00:04:03.055 --> 00:04:04.775
or Bill Gates, or Martha Stewart,

00:04:04.775 --> 00:04:07.397
or any of these entrepreneurs
that we prop on this channel,

00:04:07.397 --> 00:04:10.873
you can't do exactly what they did,

00:04:10.873 --> 00:04:12.432
because you are not them.

00:04:12.432 --> 00:04:15.709
You can take what they
did, apply the lesson,

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:17.611
and tweak it, to make it your own.

00:04:17.611 --> 00:04:19.817
And then you're going
to have that success.

00:04:19.817 --> 00:04:21.942
And so I think a lot of
entrepreneurs are really stubborn.

00:04:21.942 --> 00:04:25.332
I think that's a really
good trait a lot of times.

00:04:25.332 --> 00:04:28.168
But I think that stubbornness
can also hold us back

00:04:28.168 --> 00:04:31.999
from hearing feedback, that
can help us become better.

00:04:31.999 --> 00:04:35.277
I like to say that I'm open until I'm not.

00:04:35.277 --> 00:04:37.888
At the start of any project,
I'm really open to feedback.

00:04:37.888 --> 00:04:39.800
If I don't know what I'm doing,

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.761
I have a goal, I want
to accomplish this goal,

00:04:41.761 --> 00:04:44.612
and I don't know how to do
it, I'm very open to feedback.

00:04:44.612 --> 00:04:45.967
Do you have an idea to help me get better?

00:04:45.967 --> 00:04:47.255
Amazing, let's hear it.

00:04:47.255 --> 00:04:48.598
You're an industry expert, awesome.

00:04:48.598 --> 00:04:50.436
You've never seen this before,

00:04:50.436 --> 00:04:51.768
but you still have an opinion?

00:04:51.768 --> 00:04:52.753
I want to hear it.

00:04:52.753 --> 00:04:55.028
I'm collecting as much
information as possible,

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:56.512
until I make a decision.

00:04:56.512 --> 00:04:57.589
Until I'm certain.

00:04:57.589 --> 00:04:59.961
Until I know that this is
the path I want to take,

00:04:59.961 --> 00:05:01.443
and then I'm not open.

00:05:01.443 --> 00:05:02.276
Then I'm closed.

00:05:02.276 --> 00:05:03.933
Then I'm, this is what we're doing.

00:05:03.933 --> 00:05:06.089
At least for now, right?

00:05:06.089 --> 00:05:08.681
Like, I need to test it out like this.

00:05:08.681 --> 00:05:10.619
This is the plan, let's stick to it.

00:05:10.619 --> 00:05:12.300
If it doesn't work, we'll adjust,

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.866
but for now, I'm done with the feedback,

00:05:14.866 --> 00:05:16.340
let's take some action.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:17.370
And I think too many entrepreneurs

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.678
just hold themselves back.

00:05:18.678 --> 00:05:21.460
Either from their stubbornness,
to not taking the feedback,

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.392
or, all they do is take in the feedback,

00:05:24.392 --> 00:05:26.938
and that holds them back from
actually taking any action,

00:05:26.938 --> 00:05:28.488
because they're afraid of
being judged so harshly

00:05:28.488 --> 00:05:29.543
the next time.

00:05:29.543 --> 00:05:32.598
Use feedback as a
counselor, and not a jailer.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.431
(whoosh)

00:05:33.431 --> 00:05:34.479
So my Question of the Day today is,

00:05:34.479 --> 00:05:36.780
what was the single best piece of feedback

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:40.598
you've ever received, for your business?

00:05:40.598 --> 00:05:41.896
Leave it in the comments below,

00:05:41.896 --> 00:05:43.191
I'm going to join in the discussion,

00:05:43.191 --> 00:05:44.845
I'm super curious to see
what you guys have to say.

00:05:44.845 --> 00:05:47.005
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Peter Borstner.

00:05:47.005 --> 00:05:49.310
Peter, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:52.130
"Your One Word," it really,
really means a lot to me.

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:53.627
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:05:53.627 --> 00:05:54.911
I believe in you.

00:05:54.911 --> 00:05:57.017
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:05:57.017 --> 00:05:59.144
And whatever your one word is.

00:05:59.144 --> 00:06:01.618
Much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:06:01.618 --> 00:06:03.734
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:04.567
(funky music)

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:06.845
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:06.845 --> 00:06:10.155
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:06:10.155 --> 00:06:10.991
Hey Believe Nation,

00:06:10.991 --> 00:06:12.610
for those of you who
want a little bit more

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:15.673
about taking criticism,
here's a few bonus clips

00:06:15.673 --> 00:06:16.981
that I wanted to share with you.

00:06:16.981 --> 00:06:17.986
I hope you enjoy.

00:06:17.986 --> 00:06:20.852
- I am one who always welcomes criticism.

00:06:20.852 --> 00:06:24.479
And I encourage people, you
should welcome criticism.

00:06:24.479 --> 00:06:28.006
And be bold enough to give criticism.

00:06:28.006 --> 00:06:31.716
If the criticism is
coming out of benevolence,

00:06:31.716 --> 00:06:34.250
that I want, that
someone is criticising me

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:36.583
so that I can become better.

00:06:37.941 --> 00:06:39.565
Then it is always welcome.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:42.689
But if someone is criticising
just out of jealousy,

00:06:42.689 --> 00:06:44.929
or trying to pull someone down,

00:06:44.929 --> 00:06:47.490
then that is not good.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:51.073
Then that is coming
from a malific mindset.

00:06:54.179 --> 00:06:58.956
So, constructive criticism I
feel everyone should welcome.

00:06:58.956 --> 00:07:03.388
Criticism with compassion,
criticism fits love.

00:07:03.388 --> 00:07:07.451
It's most a durability, and
it should always be welcomed.

00:07:07.451 --> 00:07:09.864
- You need to get in a community
where you can get feedback.

00:07:09.864 --> 00:07:12.097
You need either a coach who
can give you some direct,

00:07:12.097 --> 00:07:13.033
one-to-one feedback,

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:14.908
or a community of friends
you just go out with.

00:07:14.908 --> 00:07:16.393
Maybe you go to lunch
with them once a month.

00:07:16.393 --> 00:07:17.581
You share everything you're doing,

00:07:17.581 --> 00:07:18.768
they give you some feedback.

00:07:18.768 --> 00:07:21.219
Or you shoot a video, you send
that video out to everybody,

00:07:21.219 --> 00:07:22.542
get some feedback on it.

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:24.316
You create a PowerPoint?

00:07:24.316 --> 00:07:27.000
Practice if with five people
before the bit meeting.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.744
Get back in the game,

00:07:28.744 --> 00:07:29.626
where you have a community of people

00:07:29.626 --> 00:07:31.192
who are giving you advanced feedback,

00:07:31.192 --> 00:07:33.141
before you release it.

00:07:33.141 --> 00:07:35.363
Feedback before you do it,

00:07:35.363 --> 00:07:37.701
so that you get smarter at all of this.

00:07:37.701 --> 00:07:41.685
Because nothing makes a
dream come more into life

00:07:41.685 --> 00:07:44.710
than when you start getting
feedback from other people

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:47.992
about your movement toward
the dream, you know?

00:07:47.992 --> 00:07:49.695
And before I shoot a big sales video

00:07:49.695 --> 00:07:51.281
for one of my online courses,

00:07:51.281 --> 00:07:53.976
I'll send it out to 15, 20
people, and get feedback,

00:07:53.976 --> 00:07:56.468
and then I'll often go re-shoot it again.

00:07:56.468 --> 00:07:58.408
Or I'll put it out into my community,

00:07:58.408 --> 00:08:00.390
and I'll see the clips and
the conversions and say,

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:02.754
it's not, let's do it again.

00:08:02.754 --> 00:08:05.421
And it's that willingness to get feedback,

00:08:05.421 --> 00:08:06.911
that will keep your dream alive,

00:08:06.911 --> 00:08:09.963
because if it's just in your mind,

00:08:09.963 --> 00:08:11.135
and you're just doing it by yourself,

00:08:11.135 --> 00:08:14.712
but you never actually
get a positive community,

00:08:14.712 --> 00:08:17.267
giving you constructive
feedback towards it.

00:08:17.267 --> 00:08:21.094
It will never be in the social realm.

00:08:21.094 --> 00:08:22.499
And when it is in the social realm,

00:08:22.499 --> 00:08:24.744
it feels more real, you know?

00:08:24.744 --> 00:08:25.676
When people actually comment.

00:08:25.676 --> 00:08:27.734
It's one thing to be an artist,

00:08:27.734 --> 00:08:30.020
and in your studio painting
for yourself all day.

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:31.366
That's great.

00:08:31.366 --> 00:08:33.039
But once you get some feedback on it,

00:08:33.039 --> 00:08:34.055
and constructive feedback,

00:08:34.055 --> 00:08:38.222
you get that self-awareness,
and that social awareness,

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:41.704
to contribute and create at another level.

00:08:41.704 --> 00:08:45.980
- Experience in your
business is important.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:48.328
But is experience is a bias.

00:08:48.328 --> 00:08:51.331
And much of the biases people have

00:08:51.331 --> 00:08:55.081
from understanding a
business, is not useful.

00:08:56.139 --> 00:08:59.066
And I was going back to
what useful advice to give.

00:08:59.066 --> 00:09:02.983
So I always say, have
some people on your team,

00:09:05.194 --> 00:09:08.096
who understand they not see you are

00:09:08.096 --> 00:09:09.929
angering or attacking,

00:09:11.051 --> 00:09:14.498
but be driven by original thinking.

00:09:14.498 --> 00:09:17.389
And what's more important than experience,

00:09:17.389 --> 00:09:18.982
is the rate of learning.

00:09:18.982 --> 00:09:19.815
- Right.

00:09:19.815 --> 00:09:22.610
- Some entrepreneurs I find,

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:25.233
respond negatively to critique.

00:09:25.233 --> 00:09:27.459
I think entrepreneurs
should look for critique,

00:09:27.459 --> 00:09:31.223
and people who agree with you
are not being useful to you.

00:09:31.223 --> 00:09:32.669
- Well you know, I have to say, you know,

00:09:32.669 --> 00:09:34.709
all that criticism that came out,

00:09:34.709 --> 00:09:37.967
it ended up being kind of a good thing.

00:09:37.967 --> 00:09:40.071
Because one of the things
that I wanted to do,

00:09:40.071 --> 00:09:43.577
was I wanted to actually
start a conversation,

00:09:43.577 --> 00:09:46.503
about slavery, about America's role in it.

00:09:46.503 --> 00:09:48.344
And to actually take an audience member

00:09:48.344 --> 00:09:49.701
from the 21st Century,

00:09:49.701 --> 00:09:51.513
and stick them in the Antebellum South,

00:09:51.513 --> 00:09:55.531
and have a sense of what
America was like back then.

00:09:55.531 --> 00:09:58.575
And, so even the people that
have criticized the movie,

00:09:58.575 --> 00:09:59.911
and a lot of people don't like it,

00:09:59.911 --> 00:10:02.849
and I can understand, though
a lot of people do like it.

00:10:02.849 --> 00:10:05.045
And they've been kind
of going back-and-forth.

00:10:05.045 --> 00:10:08.607
And that back-and-forth is
really what I really wanted

00:10:08.607 --> 00:10:09.991
for the end of the day of this movie,

00:10:09.991 --> 00:10:13.160
and I hope that continues
for the next few years.

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:14.834
- [Audience Member] If you have ever dealt

00:10:14.834 --> 00:10:16.579
with self-criticism in writing, and if so,

00:10:16.579 --> 00:10:18.829
how have you dealt with it?

00:10:21.767 --> 00:10:23.329
- Well I deal with it every day.

00:10:23.329 --> 00:10:26.829
You want it to be the best that it can be.

00:10:27.803 --> 00:10:30.867
And so, my assumption is always,

00:10:30.867 --> 00:10:34.704
that what I've written
first needs to be improved,

00:10:34.704 --> 00:10:38.871
and sometimes, when it's really
bad, it has to be scrapped.

00:10:38.871 --> 00:10:41.283
I'm not sure that's what you mean.

00:10:41.283 --> 00:10:44.303
The process that I go through with a book

00:10:44.303 --> 00:10:47.803
is first draft, second draft, polish, and,

00:10:50.237 --> 00:10:52.710
I can polish every day's work,

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:55.877
so that I can produce a clean manuscript

00:10:55.877 --> 00:10:58.693
at the end of X number of months.

00:10:58.693 --> 00:11:02.681
Or in the case of a book like "11/22/63,"

00:11:02.681 --> 00:11:06.848
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:11:07.754 --> 00:11:09.002
A little bit longer but, you know,

00:11:09.002 --> 00:11:10.650
that was like historical novel,

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:12.521
and that was a lot like work.

00:11:12.521 --> 00:11:14.061
(audience laughing)

00:11:14.061 --> 00:11:17.394
And I still got this huge stack of books

00:11:18.486 --> 00:11:22.193
about the 60s, and Kennedy,
and Oswald in the corner.

00:11:22.193 --> 00:11:25.488
And I don't even try to look
at it, it gives me the horrors.

00:11:25.488 --> 00:11:26.321
(audience laughing)

00:11:26.321 --> 00:11:27.441
But you have to be careful,

00:11:27.441 --> 00:11:31.608
and you have to be willing to
take outside criticism too.

00:11:32.678 --> 00:11:36.511
From editors, and the
more successful you are,

00:11:38.421 --> 00:11:42.535
the more you need to try
to do the right thing.

00:11:42.535 --> 00:11:44.267
That's all I can say.

00:11:44.267 --> 00:11:45.233
- [Audience Member] Thank you.

